<header class="kube-library-header">
  <div class="kube-library-container">
    <p class="kube-label">The KubeDaily workshop</p>
    <h1>Less theory.<br /><span>More hands-on understanding.</span></h1>
    <p class="kube-library-intro">Explore containers and Kubernetes at your own pace. Start with Docker, inspect a workload, and build up to packaging applications with Helm.</p>
    <div class="kube-library-links"><a href="/labs/Learn-Docker/">Start with Docker →</a><a href="/blog/">Looking for an explanation? Read the guides →</a></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section id="lab-library" class="kube-library-container kube-library-section" data-content-library>
  <div class="kube-library-toolbar">
    <div><p class="kube-label">Practice & explore</p><h2>Choose your next lab</h2></div>
    <div class="kube-library-search" hidden data-library-controls>
      <label for="lab-search">Find a lab</label>
      <input id="lab-search" type="search" placeholder="Search Docker, kubectl, Helm…" data-library-search />
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="kube-library-count" role="status" data-library-count><%= length(@labs) %> labs to explore</p>
  <div class="kube-labs-grid">
    <%= for lab <- @labs do %>
      <article class="kube-lab-card" data-library-card>
        <div class="kube-lab-card-top"><span class="kube-lab-number" aria-hidden="true">&gt;_</span><p class="kube-label"><%= lab["category"] %></p></div>
        <h3><a href={"/labs/#{lab["id"]}/"}><%= lab["title"] %></a></h3>
        <p><%= lab["description"] %></p>
        <div class="kube-lab-card-tags" aria-label="Topics"><%= for tag <- Enum.take(lab["tags"], 3) do %><span><%= tag %></span><% end %></div>
        <a class="kube-lab-card-link" href={"/labs/#{lab["id"]}/"}>Open lab <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <p class="kube-library-empty" hidden data-library-empty>No labs match that search. Try a tool name or clear the search to see everything.</p>
  <div class="kube-library-practice"><strong>A good lab habit</strong><p>Use a disposable environment. Check your cluster context, read commands before running them, and clean up the resources you create.</p></div>
</section>

<section class="kube-library-container kube-library-footer">
  <div><p class="kube-label">Learn in the open</p><h2>Make the next step easier for someone.</h2><p>Report an outdated command, clarify a prerequisite, or contribute an exercise.</p></div>
  <a href="https://github.com/kubernetesdaily/kubernetesdaily.github.io/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Improve a lab →</a>
</section>
